"""Declared uses of unscoped managers outside tests (guard G2 in
docs/ARCHITECTURE-tenant-sharding.md section 4.1). Read by
`tests/test_unscoped_query_sites_are_declared.py`.

Why: `TenantManager` filters soft deletes only, so `Model.objects` is already
unscoped by tenant. What the viewset contract test cannot see is service,
Celery and signal code that reaches past the manager entirely. This file lists
every such site the AST scanner finds, with the reason it is safe today; after
a database split each of them needs a routing decision.

Entry: (file under backend/, expression, count, tag, reason) -- one row per (file, expression, tag)
  expression  `X.all_objects`, `X._base_manager`, `X._default_manager`, `Tenant.objects`
  count       how many times that expression occurs in that file under that tag
  reason      why those uses are safe. Where one row covers uses with different reasons they are
              joined with ` ‖ `, each prefixed `function: ` -- the function the use sat in when the
              reason was written. That prefix is a pointer for the reader; nothing checks it.

The key had the enclosing "Class.function" in it until 2026-11-13 (user decision): renaming or moving a
function turned the guard red with nothing about tenancy changed (103 commits touched this file in six
weeks). The function is no longer part of the key, so a rename inside a file is silent. Still red: a new
expression in a file, one more or one fewer use of a declared expression (the count), a changed
expression, a use moved to another file, a row whose uses are gone. The scanner cannot see a tag, so
the count it checks is the sum over the tags of one (file, expression).

Tags (what keeps the site from leaking across tenants today):
  LOCK      lock / re-read of ONE row by pk that the caller already reached through a
            scoped path; `all_objects` only skips the soft-delete filter
  PK        lookup keyed by a pk / FK of an already scoped row
  FILTERED  carries its own tenant filter, or is wrapped in scope_to_tenant
  CODE      lookup by a code, then checked / relied on to be unique
  GLOBAL    model has no tenant column
  FANOUT    the Tenant table itself: fan-out, or resolving one tenant by code / id
  CROSS     deliberately crosses tenants (dispatch, residence, ADMIN, joint bench)
  CLI       management command / maintenance sweep with no request or tenant

To declare a NEW site you must add its row here, with a reason that says why it
cannot return or change another tenant's rows -- or, if it can, that it is meant to.
A row whose site no longer exists must be deleted.
"""

